  }))), "Related work and State of the Art Approaches"), mdx("p", null, "Chain-of-Thought (CoT) prompting has been shown to\nsignificantly improve the ability of large language\nmodels to perform complex reasoning by generating\nexplicit intermediate steps before producing an answer\n", "[Wei et al., 2022]", ".\nHowever, CoT introduces two major types of costs that\nare especially problematic in multilingual and\nlow-resource settings. "), mdx("p", null, "First, manual-CoT (few-shot, human-written reasoning demonstrations)\nrequire tedious, task-specific annotations that do not\neasily generalize across new domains or languages ", "[Wei et al., 2022; Zhang et al., 2022]", ".\nSecond, verbose CoT rationales dramatically increase inference cost:\noutputs can be an order of magnitude longer than direct answers,\ninflating token usage, latency,\nand, in multilingual cases, amplifying error propagation through translation and script mixing ", "[Xu et al., 2025; Han et al., 2025]", "."), mdx("p", null, "To reduce these costs, prior work has explored several directions."), mdx("p", null, " (a) Automatic demonstration generation,\nincluding Auto-CoT ", "[Zhang et al., 2022]", ",\nConsistency-based Self-Adaptive Prompting (COSP) ", "[Wan et al., 2023]", ",\nand Universal Self-Adaptive Prompting (USP) ", "[Wan et al., 2023]", ",\neliminates the need for human-authored CoT exemplars\nby having models generate or refine their own demonstrations.", mdx("br", null), "\n(b) Concise reasoning methods,\nsuch as Chain-of-Draft (CoD) ", "[Xu et al., 2025]", ",\nZero-shot CoT ", "[Tojima et al, 2022]", "\nand Token-Budget-Aware LLM Reasoning (TALE)\n", "[Han et al., 2025]", ",\nexplicitly aim to compress, constrain,\nor otherwise shape model rationales to reduce inference cost\nwhile preserving accuracy.", mdx("br", null), "\n(c) Adaptive computation and uncertainty-aware decoding,\nincluding RouteLLM ", "[Ong et al., 2024]", ",\nMixture-of-Experts gating strategies ", "[Li et al., 2023]", ",\nand Contrastive Decoding variants ", "[Li et al., 2023]", ",\nseek to minimize compute by selectively allocating reasoning effort\nor stabilizing token choices through contrastive expert - base model reweighting."), mdx("p", null, "Despite this progress,\nvery little of this literature examines CoT in multilingual\nor low-resource languages,\nand even less addresses the unique challenges these languages pose.\nMoreover, existing efficient CoT methods assume high-resource training conditions\nand well-calibrated reasoning behavior,\nwhich do not hold for low-resource languages like Nepali."), mdx("h2", {
